meta {
  name: Review Alert
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/llm/review/AAPL?direction=UP&timeframe=M5&price=336.05
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  direction: UP
  timeframe: M5
  price: 336.05
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # LLM Review Alert (on-demand)

  Runs the SAME multi-timeframe LLM alert review the async pipeline runs when a
  real alert fires — but synchronously, for any symbol/direction you choose. Use
  it to inspect and tune the review context + verdict without waiting for a live
  alert. It also writes the same EOD artifacts (the [ALERT_LLM_REVIEW] log line
  and a JSON sidecar under logs/alert-reviews/), so it is a faithful dry-run.

  Uses the review model from app.alert-review.model (default qwen3:14b), so it is
  slower than the live /analyze endpoint — allow 10-60s.

  ## Path
  - `{ticker}` — any US symbol.

  ## Query
  - `direction` — the alert direction to review: UP or DOWN (default UP).
  - `timeframe` — the notional alert timeframe label (default M5).
  - `price`     — optional alert price label.

  ## What it gathers (distilled, never raw bars)
  Multi-timeframe snapshot via BarDataManager — D, M60, M30, M1 — each with the
  current Supertrend (direction, line, ATR separation, flip count) and the EMA
  stack. Bars use the configured app.engine.trading-sessions. The `context` field
  in the response is exactly what the model saw.

  ## Response (200)
  { ticker, alertDirection, timeframe, model, reviewEnabled,
    context,                     // the distilled multi-TF briefing (plain text)
    verdict: {
      conviction (1..maxConviction),  // strength of evidence FOR the alert direction
      confidence (HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW),
      alignment  (ALIGNED|MIXED|CONFLICTING),
      supportingFactors[], riskFactors[], rationale,
      nextDirections: [ { direction (BULLISH|BEARISH|SIDEWAYS), trigger,
                          rationale, likelihood (HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW) } ],
      ok, note
    },
    timestamp }

  - `ok=false` → fail-safe (LLM disabled/down/bad output); `note` explains why.
  - Requires app.llm.enabled=true and a reachable runtime with the review model
    pulled (ollama pull qwen3:14b).

  ## Advisory only
  The review is logged for analysis — it never places or blocks an order.
}
